{
  "version": 1,
  "methodology": [
    "Expectations were written from the guides that exist in knowledge/ (page ids, titles, aliases), not from engine output. A handful of probes (machine learning, ml, merge pdf, compress an image, how do i write a good prompt, machien learning, embeding, redact api keys from logs) were run first to find the known weaknesses named in the brief; those queries are included and marked in the report as 'seen before authoring'.",
    "Fields: q = query. c = category. s = subject area. conf = 'confident' (engine must give a confident answer that is one of 'a'), 'weak' (engine must NOT give a confident answer), 'any' (no requirement on confidence, but if a confident answer is given it must be one of 'a' when 'a' is non-empty).",
    "a = acceptable confident answers (page ids). n = pages of which at least one must be visible in the first 6 surfaced guides (answer + cluster + learn-more + closest pages). cover = {ids, min}: at least 'min' of these guides must be visible in the first 6 (used for broad topics that have no single guide).",
    "t = tools that must be recommended. ta = extra tools that are acceptable but not required. Any recommended tool outside t + ta is a false-positive tool recommendation. Omitted t/ta means no tool is expected.",
    "lm = at least one of these ids must appear in the 'learn more' list. rw = rewrite kind the engine should report ('typo', 'abbreviation', 'framing').",
    "A query counts as 'protected' when the unmodified engine already passes every check for it; that set is frozen in tests/data/search-relevance-baseline.json and may not regress."
  ],
